[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The desk's own cause table
says otherwise. Read row by row, with the note under it, it holds three problems, and the queued
parser fix closes one of them. Each problem now has its own ticket, and each report is in one of
them: the parser ticket leaves out the one-day moves, which the table counts under `parser` and
names in its note.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, three tickets. The parser fix leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | where the table counts it | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the `parser` row, less the one-day moves in the note | [#1](https://github.com/garrettmosrie/what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| `hint` | the `hint` row, which has no ticket of its own until now | [#2](https://github.com/garrettmosrie/what-it-shows/issues/2) |
| `one-day` | the note under the table: read as a one-day move, filed under `parser` by tenant | [#4](https://github.com/garrettmosrie/what-it-shows/issues/4) |

Each report is placed by its tenant, channel and booking form (`causes.ts`), not by the tag intake
gave it. The tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, and the table shows how often it disagrees.

## The three problems

### `parser`: the shared parser reads day-first dates month first

Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. The shared parser reads every date month first, so a
booking for 7 April goes out for 4 July. Only dates whose day is 12 or less can flip, which is why
it looks random from the outside. This is the bug #4471 was opened for, and the queued fix is for
it. Ticket [#1](https://github.com/garrettmosrie/what-it-shows/issues/1).

### `hint`: booking-v3's form tells day-first tenants to type month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. At a day-first tenant, people type what the
hint says, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. The symptom is the same
swap, but the code is different: the parser fix does not touch it. Only reports that came in
through the form at a booking-v3 tenant have it. Ticket
[#2](https://github.com/garrettmosrie/what-it-shows/issues/2).

### `one-day`: dates that move by one day

Some reports are not a swap at all. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May."
(R-41202). A day/month swap cannot move a date by one day, so this is a different bug. It looks
like a time-zone conversion: one meeting showed Tuesday to a client in Lisbon and Monday to a
client in Toronto (R-41344). The desk spotted these (`desk-notes.json`); the table counts them
under `parser`, where they are filed, and names them in the note. They belong here, not in #1. Ticket
[#4](https://github.com/garrettmosrie/what-it-shows/issues/4).

## What changes on the desk

- #4471 keeps `parser`. New `hint` reports go to #2, one-day moves to #4.
- Place a report by tenant, channel and form, not by intake's tag.

